      "updated_at": "2025-12-05T03:09:45Z",
      "body": "Hello! That's a great question!\nI noticed that neither your preprocessing pipeline nor the one described in the paper mentions z-score scaling. Therefore, before reproducing Figure 2, I wondered if this step was actually required but overlooked and unmentioned in the paper\u2014and since you didn\u2019t perform it either, it might have led to a significant deviation in the evaluation scores.\nInitially, I hypothesized that applying scaling would be necessary to achieve the results reported in the paper, and the suboptimal performance you encountered was due to omitting this step. To investigate the root cause, I prepared two sets of datasets during preprocessing:\n\n1. One set with z-score scaling applied to both the training and test datasets;\n\n2. The other set without z-score scaling for both the training and test datasets.\n\nI trained two models separately using these datasets and conducted predictions, but the results were completely opposite to my expectations!The dataset with scaling yielded evaluation results similar to what you observed, while the dataset without scaling produced results consistent with those in the original paper.\nThus, I now wonder if the preprocessing steps in the paper are rigorous and scaling is truly unnecessary\u2014and could it be that you actually applied scaling?",
